The v5 slide face stores one form for every authenticated rebase, but the
donor consumers read the cache data through two incompatible contracts, and
r91's poison slot pins the split to the mapping writability.

Read-only auth mappings (sc25 mapping[5], initProt 1) hold GOT-style slots
that the dyld fixup stage authenticates (AUTDA, the r86b wall-85 family):
they need the full hardware pacda form, PAC at bits 38-55.  Writable data
mappings (sc25 mapping[4], initProt 3) hold ObjC-managed slots (the
metaclass self-reference family, diversity 0x6ae1): libobjc reads those
raw and its own stores keep only bits 3-46 ("pacda x17, x16; and
#0x7ffffffffffff8; str" at libobjc+0x1b4b4/1b51c in the 24A446 cache), so
any bits above 46 are garbage to it.  r87 made this face sign every
authenticated entry at full width, which poisons the writable-mapping
family exactly as observed in r89-r91: far = [VA36][PAC bits 38-43]
[zeroed 44+], VA part bit-exact across three generations.

Scope the r87 signature to the read-only mappings and store the writable
mappings plain (the donor's jop_key==0 gate behaviour, which sheng's
9b19ac2 reversal also restored globally).  A sheng-v5 probe row reports
the writability, diversity and stored value of the first eight
authenticated entries so the next window shows the split in place.

